          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The operations on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-space"} H-space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (such as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            or a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            this is known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+ring"} Pontrjagin ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_*(X)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToWhiteheadProduct Relation to Whitehead product
          %p
            Under the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+homomorphism"} Hurewicz homomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutator"} commutator
            of the Pontrjagin product on homology is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+product"} Whitehead product
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/based+loop+space"} based loop space
          %p
            This is due to
            %a{:href => "#Samelson53"} Samelson (1953)
            and for higher Whitehead brackets due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Arkowitz71"} Arkowitz (1971)
          %p
            In fact, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+ring"} Pontrjagin ring
            structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/based+loop+spaces"} based loop spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
            is identified via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+homomorphism"} Hurewicz homomorphism
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+algebra"} universal enveloping algebra
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "universal+enveloping+algebra#ForSuperLieAlgebras"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+bracket+super+Lie+algebra"} Whitehead bracket super Lie algebra
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#MilnorMoore65"}> Milnor &amp; Moore (1965) Appendix
            ;
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Whitehead78"} Whitehead (1978) Thm. X.7.10
            = succeed "&rbrack;." do
              %a{:href => "#FélixHalperinThomas00"} Félix, Halperin &amp; Thomas 2000, Thm. 16.13
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} hence
            the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            may be read off from any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (by the proposition
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Sullivan+model+of+loop+space#SullivanModelForBasedLoopSpace"} here
          %p For the following examples we use these notational conventions:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
                denotes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            %li
              %p a subscript on a generator denotes its degree,
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}\langle\cdots \rangle
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕂
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} spanned
                by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
                of generators listed inside the angular brackets;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}[\cdots]
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                of the free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded-commutative+algebra"} graded-commutative algebra
                on the set of generators listed inside the square brackets;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(-)
                denotes the graded
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
                on a given
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dgc-algebra"} semifree dgc-algebra
                on a given set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\cdots\}
                of generators subject to differential relations we denote, with slight abuse of notation, by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} /
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo =
                              %mi …
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋮
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{K}[\cdots]\big/
                      \\left(
                      \\begin{array}{c}
                      \\mathrm{d}(-) = \ldots
                      \\\
                      \\vdots
                      \\end{array}
                      \\right)
          %p
          #RationalPontrAlgOfLoopsOfSpheresAndCPn.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (rational Pontrjagin algebra of loops of spheres and
                = succeed "s)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                        %msup
                          %mi P
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^n
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model+of+spheres"} Sullivan model of
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔩
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 2
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 3
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(\mathfrak{l} S^2)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{Q}\big[
                    \\omega_2, \omega_3
                    \\big]\big/
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    \\mathrm{d} \omega_2 \,=\, 0
                    \\\
                    \\mathrm{d} \omega_3
                    \\,=\,
                    \\tfrac{1}{2} \omega_2 \wedge \omega_2
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              From this it follows (since
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+co-binary+Sullivan+differential+is+the+dual+Whitehead+product"} the co-binary Sullivan differential is the dual Whitehead product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+brackets"} Whitehead
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+brackets"} super Lie brackets
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
              are:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    [v_1, v_1] = v_2
                    \\\
                    [v_2, v_2] = 0
                    \\\
                    [v_1, v_2] = 0
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              The rational Pontrjagin ring of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega S^2
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+algebra"} universal enveloping algebra
              of this
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                            %msubsup
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_\bullet\big(
                    \\Omega S^2
                    ;\,
                    \\mathbb{K}
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    T\big(
                    \\mathbb{K}\langle v_1, v_2\rangle
                    \\big)
                    \\big/
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    2 v_1^2 - v_2
                    \\\
                    v_1 v_2 - v_2 v_1
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right)
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              Therefore the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              of the Pontrjagin ring of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega S^2
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}[v_1, v_2]
              but the product of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1
              is deformed from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1 \cdot v_1 = 0
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1 \cdot v_1 = \tfrac{1}{2}v_2
            %p
              Similarly, the rational Pontrjagin algebra of the loop space of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 6
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                            %msubsup
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                              %mn 2
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 6
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 6
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 6
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_\bullet\big(
                    \\Omega S^4
                    ;\,
                    \\mathbb{K}
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    T\big( \mathbb{K}\langle v_3, v_6\rangle \big)
                    \\big/
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    2 v_3^2 - v_6
                    \\\
                    v_3 v_6 - v_6 v_3
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right)
            %p
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 6
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}[v_3, v_6]
              but with the product of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_3
              deformed from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_3 \cdot v_3 = 0
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 3
                      %mo =
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 6
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_3 \cdot v_3 = \tfrac{1}{2}v_6
            %p
              On the other hand, the differential of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model+of+complex+projective+space"} Sullivan model of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^n
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
              has vanishing co-binary part, so that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                            %msubsup
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_\bullet\big(
                    \\Omega \mathbb{C}P^{n \geq 2}
                    ;\,
                    \\mathbb{K}
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    T\big( \mathbb{K}\langle v_2, v_{2n}\rangle \big)
                    \\big/
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    2 v_1^2
                    \\\
                    v_1 v_{2n} - v_{2n} v_1
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{K}[v_1, v_{2n}]
            %p is just a plain graded-commutative algebra.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = \infty
              (ie. for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ≃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^\infty \simeq
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} /
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %msubsup
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_\bullet\big(
                    \\Omega \mathbb{C}P^{\infty}
                    ;\,
                    \\mathbb{K}
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    T\big( \mathbb{K}\langle v_2\rangle \big)
                    \\big/
                    \\big(
                    2 v_1^2
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{K}[v_1]
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
            %p
              reflecting the fact that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \, \mathbb{C}P^\infty \,\simeq\, \Omega B U(1)\,\simeq\, S^1
          %h3#homological_group_completion Homological group completion
          %p
            The homological version of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion+theorem"} group completion theorem
            relates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+ring"} Pontrjagin ring
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+monoid"} topological monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to that of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi B
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega B A
          %h3#RelationToStringTopology Relation to string topology
          %p
