            stuck to the 0-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\} \hookrightarrow X
            %a{:href => "string+topology#OpenStringProductOn0BraneIsPontrjaginProduct"} there
          %h3#RelationToQuantumCohomology Relation to quantum cohomology
          %p
            The homology Pontrjagin product of certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            is identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+cohomology"} quantum cohomology
            of corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            (see references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesOnQuantumCohomologyAsPontrjaginRings"} below
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+of+loop+spaces"} homology of loop spaces
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The concept and the terminology “Pontryagin-multiplication” is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"}> Raoul Bott
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans+Samelson"} Hans Samelson
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Pontryagin product in spaces of paths
              %strong 27
              (1953) 320–337 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02564566"}> doi:10.1007/BF02564566
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            who name it in honor of the analogous product operation on the homology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            due to:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homologies in compact Lie groups
              %strong 6
              (
              %strong> 48
              ) 3 (1939) 389–422 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://m.mathnet.ru/php/archive.phtml?wshow=paper&jrnid=sm&paperid=5835&option_lang=eng"}> mathnet:5835
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p see also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans+Samelson"}> Hans Samelson
              , §3 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Beiträge Zur Topologie der Gruppen-Mannigfaltigkeiten
              %strong 42
              5 (1941) 1091-1137 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1970463"}> jsotr:1970463
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Proof that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutator"} commutator
            of the Pontrjagin product is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+product"} Whitehead product
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+homomorphism"} Hurewicz homomorphism
          %ul
            %li#Samelson53
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans+Samelson"}> Hans Samelson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Connection Between the Whitehead and the Pontryagin Product
              %strong 75
              4 (1953) 744–752 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2372549"}> doi:10.2307/2372549
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
          %ul
