              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/based+loop+space"} based loop space
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply-connected+topological+space"} simply-connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is essentially the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+cohomology+ring"} quantum cohomology ring
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+variety"} flag variety
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexification"} complexification
              by its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+subgroup"} Borel subgroup
              is attributed (“Peterson isomorphism”) to
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dale+H.+Peterson"} Dale H. Peterson
                (notes by
                = succeed ")," do
